# ENTERPRISE ML PIPELINE & EXPERIMENTAL MODEL BUILDING PLAN
## Intelligent Public Transport Delay Prediction & Dynamic Route Optimization System

This implementation plan establishes a **fault-tolerant, zero-leakage, industry-standard Machine Learning & Dynamic Routing pipeline** for the master integrated dataset ([final_integrated_dataset.csv](file:///d:/An%20Intelligent%20Public%20Transport%20Delay%20Prediction%20and%20Route%20Optimization%20System%20Using%20Machine%20Learning/final%20yr%20dataset%20new/final%20yr%20dataset/final_integrated_dataset.csv)) spanning **729,648 rows** and **35 features** (`2022-01-01` to `2026-08-16`).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Strict Target Leakage Protocol & Zero-Leakage Assurances**:
> 1. **`actual_arrival` is strictly excluded** from all feature spaces across all models. In production inference before a bus arrives, `actual_arrival` does not exist; including it would constitute artificial arithmetic leakage ($\text{delay} = T_{\text{actual}} - T_{\text{sched}}$).
> 2. **Target Isolation**:
>    - For **Delay Regression** (`delay_minutes`), downstream features (`disruption_label`, `occupancy_status`, `occupancy_percentage`, `passenger_count`) are excluded.
>    - For **Disruption Classification** (`disruption_label`), `delay_minutes` and `actual_arrival` are excluded because `disruption_label` was constructed from delay thresholds.
>    - For **Occupancy Classification** (`occupancy_status`), `passenger_count` and `occupancy_percentage` are excluded as they represent the mathematical definition of occupancy status.
> 3. **Temporal Partitioning (No Random K-Fold)**:
>    - **Train Set (70%)**: `2022-01-01` to `2024-12-31` (~510,750 rows).
>    - **Validation Set (15%)**: `2025-01-01` to `2025-12-31` (~109,450 rows).
>    - **Out-of-Time Holdout Test Set (15%)**: `2026-01-01` to `2026-08-16` (~109,448 rows).
> 4. **Experimental Focus & Output Segregation**: FastAPI services are postponed. Every single model's trained weights, performance metrics, and evaluation/XAI plots will be saved into dedicated model subdirectories under `MODEL BUILDING\OUTPUTS\`.

